# F43 — gt-input-remap overlay for the RSDK Sonic ports (device-verified fix).
# The shim's v1 index-remap cross-swaps physical faces vs. gptk button names
# on h700: physical A(south)=gptk `b`, B(east)=gptk `a`, X(west)=gptk `y`,
# Y(north)=gptk `x` (device trace, 2026-08-28). RSDK's shared action map has
# only two jump actions (A=jump, C=jump; B=pause; X/Y/Z=nothing), so to get
# the physical A+B faces jumping with DISTINCT keys (no duplicate-key
# crash class) we bind them to this game's RSDK-A and RSDK-C keys. X/Y are
# deliberately left unmapped — only two jump keys exist to bind. The
# RSDK-A/RSDK-C keys differ per game (separate [Keyboard 1] tables); this
# file is Sonic 1's. back=esc is kept, not repurposed, to preserve a quit path.
#
# F48 (device gate, 2026-09-01): the shim now applies the Nintendo/Xbox layout
# swap dynamically from GT_CONTROLLER_LAYOUT, so a/b are set to the Nintendo
# baseline (a<->b swapped vs the original F43 assignment) — menu-confirm
# (RSDK-A) lands on the physical A/right face under the default, and the shim
# flips it to Xbox on demand. So gptk `a`->RSDK-A key, `b`->RSDK-C key.
back = esc
start = enter
b = c
a = z
up = up
down = down
left = left
right = right
